@startuml lling-pipeline-usage
' The correction pipeline as a sequence of layers that transform one lattice,
' traced on the worked example “teh quikc brwon fox”. Layer 1 tokenizes the text
' into a single-path lattice; layer 2 (liblevenshtein) adds fuzzy alternatives at
' every position, so the lattice acquires multiple paths; layer 3 optionally drops
' ungrammatical paths; layer 4 (libgrammstein) rescores every surviving path by
' fluency, and the best-scoring path is emitted. Colour encodes the role of each
' stage: tokenize/emit slate, spelling blue, grammar filter purple, LM green.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/lling-pipeline-usage.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/integration/lling-llang/pipeline-usage.md
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Correction pipeline — four layers transforming one lattice

rectangle "**Input text**\n“teh quikc brwon fox”" as in #455A64

rectangle "**Layer 1: Tokenization**\nconvert text to an initial lattice with one path\n[“teh”, “quikc”, “brwon”, “fox”]" as tok #455A64

rectangle "**Layer 2: Spelling Correction**  (liblevenshtein)\nadd fuzzy-matching alternatives at each position\n\nPosition 0:  teh   → [the, tea, ten, …]\nPosition 1:  quikc → [quick, quack, …]\nPosition 2:  brwon → [brown, brawn, …]\nPosition 3:  fox   → [fox]  (correct)\n\nthe lattice now has multiple paths" as spell #1565C0

rectangle "**Layer 3: Grammar Filter**  (optional)\nremove paths that violate grammar rules\ne.g. “the quack brown fox” might be filtered" as cfg #6A1B9A

rectangle "**Layer 4: Language Model**  (libgrammstein)\nrescore paths based on fluency\n\nℙ(“the quick brown fox”) = −12.3  (high)\nℙ(“tea quick brown fox”) = −18.5  (lower)\nℙ(“the quick brawn fox”) = −16.2  (medium)\n\nbest path: “the quick brown fox”" as lm #2E7D32

rectangle "**Output**\n“the quick brown fox”" as out #455A64

in --> tok
tok --> spell : EXPAND
spell --> cfg : PRUNE
cfg --> lm : REWEIGHT
lm --> out : COLLAPSE

legend top right
  | Colour | Stage |
  |<#455A64> | text ⇄ lattice (tokenize / emit) |
  |<#1565C0> | spelling — liblevenshtein edit distance |
  |<#6A1B9A> | grammar — lling-llang CFG filter |
  |<#2E7D32> | fluency — libgrammstein language model |
endlegend
@enduml
